WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.392
GPU driver installation should start with a plan.

00:00:03.392 --> 00:00:08.792
Choose a Linux distribution and kernel strategy that fit the system's purpose.

00:00:08.792 --> 00:00:14.192
Long-term support distributions often favor stability and predictable updates.

00:00:14.192 --> 00:00:21.460
Rolling releases may provide newer kernels and libraries sooner, but they can also introduce more change.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:26.860
AI systems that support real workflows usually benefit from controlled change.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:31.014
Repository packages and vendor packages each have tradeoffs.

00:00:31.014 --> 00:00:37.590
Distribution packages may integrate cleanly with the package manager and kernel update process.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:41.951
Vendor packages may provide newer support or specific versions.

00:00:41.951 --> 00:00:49.013
Mixing sources without a plan can create dependency conflicts or unclear ownership of installed files.

00:00:49.013 --> 00:00:51.297
Pick an approach and document it.

00:00:51.297 --> 00:00:55.174
Version control for the stack is operational discipline.

00:00:55.174 --> 00:01:06.596
Record the distribution version, kernel, driver, firmware, CUDA or ROCm components, container runtime, inference runtime, Python environment, and relevant libraries.

00:01:06.596 --> 00:01:09.711
Pin versions when the system needs stability.

00:01:09.711 --> 00:01:17.257
Avoid unnecessary upgrades on stable AI systems unless there is a clear reason, test plan, and rollback path.

00:01:17.257 --> 00:01:20.165
Build a repeatable installation checklist.

00:01:20.165 --> 00:01:34.979
Include prerequisites, kernel headers, package sources, driver install method, Secure Boot considerations, runtime libraries, container configuration, validation commands, smoke tests, and backup or snapshot steps.

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:44.809
A checklist reduces guesswork and makes it possible to rebuild the same acceleration stack after a disk failure, migration, or failed upgrade.
